1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,120
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:06,201
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,760
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,937
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,440
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:15,697
We'll get past every wall that's
in our wake, go without hesitation!

7
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,820
Hands up!

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,217
To get to the answers we're looking for.

10
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,737
We came to this new world believing That

11
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,957
surely someday we just might find the way.

12
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,297
Our bonds won't waver.

14
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,880
Let's head on towards

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,697
A bright new future.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

18
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,597
Sing about what you are dreaming.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,217
Always stand up.

20
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,397
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

21
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

22
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

23
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,400
Let's head on never stopping.

24
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,337
Only look up.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,337
Keep your head up way up high.

26
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,037
Always step up.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:16,997
If waves are rough, jump to the sky.

28
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:18,797
Never give up.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,777
Our wishes, they will come together.

30
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:23,180
And lead us on for the future.

31
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:27,837
We drift on riding the waves.

32
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,717
Towards another shore day by day.

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,497
There are many meetings, many goodbyes.

34
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,840
Underneath the flag we fly.

35
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,697
I'll remember the pain within.

36
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,877
I'll keep it in my heart forever.

37
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:47,977
And never take it lightly.

38
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,837
But I won't surrender.

39
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom I will keep in mind.

40
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,637
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

41
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

42
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,517
Sing about what you are dreaming.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,177
Always stand up.

44
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,337
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

45
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,897
Gotta keep up.

46
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,237
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,700
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:14,317
Only look up, keep your
head up, way up high.

49
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,937
Always step up, if brains
are rough, jump to the sky.

50
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:21,637
Never give up, our wishes,
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:24,140
And lead us on for the future.

52
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,120
Hands up.

53
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:34,740
Yep, sure looks like a warship.

54
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:38,880
So, the navy's on the
island? What? Are you sure?

55
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:41,220
When did they get here? Hey, look!

56
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:42,479
We've got company!

57
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:47,760
Wait, I know him! Hey! Hello?

58
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:49,940
What you doing here?

59
00:02:50,180 --> 00:02:51,768
You remember me, don't you?

60
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:54,022
You helped me out that one time!

61
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:56,600
Straw Hat.

62
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:58,110
He's here?

63
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:02,460
That's the guy we met at
the human shop in Sabaody.

64
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:05,780
Trafalgar Law, but why is he here?

65
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,680
Right! Traffy!

66
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:09,980
He helped me out!

67
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:12,737
You guys know, back in the
Battle of Marine Corps,

68
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:17,360
he got me off the field and treated
my wounds. He did? Yeah, sure.

69
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:19,286
He saved my life like Jinbei.

70
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:22,660
Okay, I'm gonna go talk
to him right now. Hey!

71
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:28,542
I didn't expect to run into you.

72
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:29,640
Small world, huh?

73
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:30,780
You saved me.

74
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:32,300
I owe you one. Really.

75
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,070
Vix!

76
00:03:34,153 --> 00:03:36,560
Hey, wait, uh, where'd your buddies go?

77
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:41,540
Quick, hand over Straw Hat.

78
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:43,742
Hand him over and we can escape.

79
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:46,457
He'll die without my help.

80
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:48,440
Trust me, I'm a doctor.

81
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,240
Where's my brother?

82
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:57,160
What will happen to him if he
remains in that state? Simple.

83
00:03:57,440 --> 00:04:01,857
If he keeps flailing around, the
more likely he is to open his wound.

84
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:04,740
And if that happens,
chances are he'll die.

85
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,912
He needs to rest, for two weeks at least.

86
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:09,491
Got it, or he won't heal.

87
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:12,340
I understand, and thank
you for everything.

88
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,110
Hmm.

89
00:04:15,340 --> 00:04:17,928
It looks like you pulled
through, Straw Hat.

90
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:23,020
Well, glad my treatment took, but
you don't have to thank me for it.

91
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,780
I did it on a whim, that's all.

92
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:27,920
We're not buddies.

93
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:30,540
Don't forget, we're both pirates.

94
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:33,330
I know.

95
00:04:33,413 --> 00:04:35,080
Opponents, rivals, enemies.

96
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:38,960
But enemy or not, you
still help me. So thanks.

97
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,320
This is cool.

98
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:42,097
First Team Bay and now you.

99
00:04:42,180 --> 00:04:44,437
I'm getting a lot of thank
yous checked off my list.

100
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:47,680
Hey, over there, on the ground, a Marine!

101
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:54,260
Is that who I think it is?

102
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:56,797
Can I get a little help here, Trafalgar?

103
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:57,710
Hey!

104
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:00,420
Wait! Please!

105
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:07,180
Oh, no.

106
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,190
Smoker!

107
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:12,010
Smoking!

108
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:13,970
Marines!

109
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:16,640
Wait, that girl! I know her!

110
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:22,680
Luffy, we got Marines headed our way! Yep!

111
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:26,020
What do you see? What happened?

112
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:28,067
You think smoking's alright?

113
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:33,920
Please wake up!

114
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,737
That's what I thought!

115
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:39,077
It's Smokey and his crew!

116
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:40,340
Long time no see!

117
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:46,660
There's a hole in his chest.

118
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:48,960
Smoker, no!

119
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:53,960
In order to become a member
of the Seven Warlords,

120
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:58,037
he delivered the hearts of a hundred
pirates to the Navy Headquarters.

121
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:59,340
He's off the rails!

122
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:14,820
Damn you,

123
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:15,980
damn you,

124
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:18,517
damn you, damn you,

125
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:25,220
damn you, come on, really,

126
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:27,777
I hate this kind of thing, too much drama,

127
00:06:27,860 --> 00:06:30,600
room,

128
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:44,530
Shambles.

129
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:52,660
Ah, damn, he took her down again.

130
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,597
Smokey isn't moving either.

131
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:56,080
Are they both dead?

132
00:06:56,740 --> 00:06:57,860
Once wasn't enough.

133
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,740
Please, I win again, Captain.

134
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:04,330
Loopy!

135
00:07:04,413 --> 00:07:06,280
That's our cue to get out of here!

136
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,840
Hold on. Hey, you! Traffy!

137
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:11,313
Got a question for you.

138
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:15,000
Head over to the lab, around the back.

139
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:18,934
When you get there, you'll
find what you're looking for.

140
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:20,437
We'll meet again soon.

141
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:22,873
We both have things we mean to get back.

142
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:29,880
He met me.

143
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:32,277
He's going to save me from this indignity.

144
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:34,301
I'm a former pirate, not a horse.

145
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:37,976
Let's get as far away from
those Navy Pucks as we can.

146
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:46,037
Think Smokey's going to be okay?

147
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,117
That looked rough.

148
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,847
Traffy didn't go easy on it.

149
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:54,500
Hey, look, guys, it's
Straw Hat Luffy. Fire!

150
00:07:58,140 --> 00:07:58,970
Planet!

151
00:07:59,053 --> 00:08:00,437
Don't worry about those guys.

152
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,350
Smokey's down.

153
00:08:01,433 --> 00:08:02,360
The captain, too.

154
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:13,617
Who cares about the
samurai and the breads?

155
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:14,820
Not me, I say!

156
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:17,957
More importantly, where
can I find a camera?

157
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:21,158
I gotta take some pictures
before we all change back!

158
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:22,777
Pictures of what, exactly?

159
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:25,617
Then stop making my nose bleed,
or your nose, or whatever!

160
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:30,337
If we're making demands, Nami, then unbutton
my shirt so I can show off my Mechapex!

161
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:31,460
I know it's cold!

162
00:08:31,580 --> 00:08:32,410
Hang in there!

163
00:08:32,493 --> 00:08:33,457
We can make it!

164
00:08:33,540 --> 00:08:34,917
We'll figure something out!

165
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,977
I liked it better when
you weren't so nice.

166
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:38,577
This is kind of creeping me out.

167
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:39,542
I don't get it.

168
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:42,537
Did someone play a trick
and make you switch bodies?

169
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:44,340
It's so cold without my fur!

170
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:46,481
You humans sure do have it rough!

171
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:51,820
You gotta stop. He needs help.

172
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:55,880
It's too cold.

173
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:58,517
I can't move.

174
00:08:58,600 --> 00:08:59,480
I'm freezing.

175
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:01,130
Me too.

176
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:02,797
I'm starting to get scared.

177
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:03,710
Damn it.

178
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:07,357
We shouldn't have taken the kids with
us until we figured out where to go.

179
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:11,017
On the upside, I don't feel cold
at all with Chopper's fur on.

180
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:13,577
Well, I've got enough fur
for a couple of coats.

181
00:09:13,660 --> 00:09:14,490
No way!

182
00:09:14,573 --> 00:09:15,403
That's my body!

183
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:20,960
Okay, fine, but I don't think we're gonna
find any warm clothing just lying around

184
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:23,157
Maybe there's a lodge or something.

185
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:25,840
Yeah, yeah with a mirror and a camera

186
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:28,620
And a shower would be nice

187
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:34,060
Very well, I can see we
have no other choice.

188
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:37,917
I need all of you to place a
leaf upon your heads Wait, what?

189
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,077
Why would we do that?

190
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:40,157
Don't joke, dude.

191
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:44,600
The poor kiddos are gonna collapse
from the cold Besides, what leaves?

192
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:45,737
There aren't any.

193
00:09:45,820 --> 00:09:46,677
Just look around.

194
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:47,757
There are no plants.

195
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,080
Fine. Forget leaves.

196
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:51,317
Start gathering some stones instead.

197
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:52,230
Hurry.

198
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:56,996
Okay, we'll do it, but this
had better not be a prank.

199
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,282
I'll get them for the kids, too.

200
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:07,150
Now what?

201
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:08,436
We've got the rocks.

202
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:12,537
I hope you don't do some stupid spell
like abracadabra, make it not cold.

203
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:14,580
Because I'd kill you all right.

204
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:23,610
Poof.

205
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:43,450
You do,

206
00:10:43,533 --> 00:10:49,617
you're welcome, small one.

207
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:54,517
I have not always possessed the strange
ability, but one day I ate a fruit,

208
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:56,077
an unusual one,

209
00:10:56,160 --> 00:11:00,513
and since then I have been able to
disguise myself and others as I please.

210
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:04,957
I know little of foreign clothing;
I hope this will suffice also,

211
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:06,377
due to the nature of the magic.

212
00:11:06,460 --> 00:11:09,166
The clothes will disappear
if you remove them.

213
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:15,140
He covered my boobs.

214
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:19,000
I didn't know you'd eaten
a Devil Fruit. What? Devil?

215
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,860
Hey, hold on a second.

216
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:25,860
This whole time, you had that power.

217
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,882
So why didn't you use it sooner?

218
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:32,100
I was helpless.

219
00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:37,069
That little breastband she's wearing,
I couldn't bring myself to cover it up.

220
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:38,460
Oh! Curve?

221
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:46,277
That... really...

222
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,220
itches.

223
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:51,960
Jeez, say it. I'm hurt.

224
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:54,237
Admitting that isn't going to kill you.

225
00:11:54,320 --> 00:11:57,040
I itch. Oh, hey!

226
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:59,280
Look who it is! Huh?

227
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,120
Hi, guys!

228
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,260
Hey! Hey! Yay!

229
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:06,840
Woo-hoo-hoo!

230
00:12:07,420 --> 00:12:08,737
What are they doing here?

231
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:09,650
Bye!

232
00:12:09,733 --> 00:12:10,563
Everyone okay?

233
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,260
Woo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

234
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:15,740
Dude, now what?

235
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:17,160
Hey, it's Luffy!

236
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,880
Zoro and Usopp, too! Robin!

237
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:23,300
I'm so happy to see you! What the?

238
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:26,177
Why's the jackass cook
prancing around like that?

239
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:28,731
You've called us strange things to people.

240
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,277
Is it just me?

241
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:34,713
Are there giant children with them, too?

242
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:40,170
Wait!

243
00:12:40,253 --> 00:12:42,900
No, don't do it! Franky! Down, boy!

244
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:48,980
Out of the cold, finally.

245
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:52,057
This building reminds me
a lot of the other one.

246
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:56,257
But this one is badly damaged, as if
there were some sort of explosion here.

247
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:59,397
Long as it gets us out of that
blizzard, it's fine by me.

248
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:01,940
Now, let's talk. Who's up first?

249
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:05,540
I can't believe I did that to my own body.

250
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:07,704
Here, let me see if I can help.

251
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:10,960
What are you doing, Saatchi?

252
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,520
Get your hands off me!

253
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:14,860
But it's me, Chopper!

254
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:21,400
My legs are back.

255
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:22,940
I'm almost told now.

256
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:26,640
My extra legs!

257
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:28,660
I'm on a set already!

258
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:34,830
Enough!

259
00:13:34,913 --> 00:13:37,429
You are never a centaur,
so just let it go!

260
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:38,940
How very odd.

261
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:46,260
Quite a funny chap, isn't he?

262
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:47,937
The skeleton...

263
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:48,920
...is talking.

264
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:53,050
Hey!

265
00:13:53,133 --> 00:13:53,963
Do a trick!

266
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:55,375
Yeah, the tank thing!

267
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:00,820
Not now!

268
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,030
Right.

269
00:14:03,113 --> 00:14:04,000
That's not him.

270
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:09,200
You sure?

271
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:12,260
You've got to be craving one. Go on.

272
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:14,877
I know you like to smoke
when you're stressed out.

273
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:16,240
So, smoke. Right.

274
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:19,361
First up, we're gonna need
to know who's who here.

275
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:21,180
Franky, got that?

276
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:22,240
Not Chopper.

277
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:25,080
You get hurt, I'm useless. Remember that.

278
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:26,928
Hey guys, Chopper speaking.

279
00:14:27,260 --> 00:14:29,620
If you have any injuries, come to me.

280
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:32,000
I'm Nami, okay?

281
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:35,060
No laser beams, no tanks, don't ask.

282
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:40,417
And now I present to you...

283
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:42,440
Nami! Yeah!

284
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:45,180
Hello, beautiful!

285
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:49,060
Defile my body again, I dare you!

286
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:51,340
I'll stop, I promise!

287
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:54,217
Please don't hurt Nami
again, she's too pretty!

288
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,260
No, don't do it!

289
00:14:55,440 --> 00:14:56,734
That would be suicide!

290
00:14:58,300 --> 00:15:00,080
Touch me and you get a fine.

291
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:01,580
100,000 berries.

292
00:15:01,820 --> 00:15:03,100
No, make it two.

293
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:04,340
But my dream!

294
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:07,450
Shut up!

295
00:15:07,620 --> 00:15:10,149
Wouldn't be so funny
if it happened to you!

296
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:15,497
Let's start from the top and
make sure we've got it straight.

297
00:15:15,580 --> 00:15:18,780
This head and legs
belong to a Wano samurai.

298
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:21,557
The distress signal we
intercepted before coming to

299
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:24,557
the island was actually meant
for the big boss crocotar.

300
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:26,464
and was sent by one of his men.

301
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:29,457
Seems our sliced-up samurai
pal did some slicing

302
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:32,422
of his own with the centaurs
on the receding end.

303
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:36,440
Yes, I fought them, but
only to rescue my son.

304
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:38,013
His name is Momonosuke.

305
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:41,600
He's missing, and those men
were in my way. Just look!

306
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:43,657
You can see with your own eyes how many

307
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:46,217
children were prisoners
in that foul facility.

308
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:48,535
I have no doubt my son is one of them.

309
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:50,440
Yeah, there were others.

310
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:52,140
More children like us.

311
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:56,140
I guess your son could be one
of them, but I don't know.

312
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:59,740
Right, but what happened
after that distress signal?

313
00:15:59,980 --> 00:16:01,560
Who the heck sliced you?

314
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:03,700
The man we encountered, him!

315
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:09,000
The one with the cold eyes and the
silly cap who bears the title Warlord.

316
00:16:11,100 --> 00:16:11,930
What?

317
00:16:12,260 --> 00:16:13,520
Wait, Traffy?

318
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:16,540
He's a Warlord now, really? Yes.

319
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:19,160
Well, a lot can change in two years.

320
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:22,740
Bastard, he took his
blade and carved me up.

321
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:27,297
My head was kept in the facility.

322
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:29,817
My torso remained where it fell.

323
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:33,320
And my legs were chased
away by a vile beast.

324
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,737
They were making a
valiant effort to escape.

325
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:38,880
But they became stuck on something.

326
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:41,317
Which was the dragon.

327
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:42,600
That explains it.

328
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:45,237
Oh, right, a warlord.

329
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:46,337
You were mad at one.

330
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:47,457
I remember now.

331
00:16:47,540 --> 00:16:49,177
Wait, but it was just legs?

332
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:50,717
So how did he talk?

333
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,080
That's a real good question.

334
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:55,880
It's simple.

335
00:16:56,300 --> 00:16:57,420
By farting.

336
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,720
It's a talent of mine.
Here, I'll show you.

337
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:04,260
Fart talking?

338
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:06,180
Okay, gross. But useful.

339
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:09,500
Didn't smell so bad outside.

340
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:13,734
Would you believe I met another
partial person recently?

341
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:16,400
You have a head and legs.

342
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:17,736
He just had a torso.

343
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:18,857
That's Fanny.

344
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:21,960
Right, because that
was his torso, dumbass.

345
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:23,480
Oh, dear!

346
00:17:23,940 --> 00:17:25,720
You saw it, skeleton? Truly?

347
00:17:26,060 --> 00:17:27,119
Where is my torso?

348
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:28,931
We must go there at once!

349
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:32,620
The whole heart thing.

350
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:34,960
You doing okay without one?

351
00:17:35,180 --> 00:17:36,540
I think so.

352
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:39,097
Talking to her is hard enough, but...

353
00:17:39,180 --> 00:17:41,657
There was a ship hidden
beside the laboratory.

354
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:45,100
The letters CC were written on it. What?

355
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:46,957
I didn't know there was a ship?

356
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:48,511
You saw it, Vice Admiral?

357
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:49,770
Yeah,

358
00:17:49,853 --> 00:17:53,137
if it was left over from the old
days before the island was destroyed,

359
00:17:53,220 --> 00:17:56,440
the mark should be PH for Punk Hazard.

360
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:00,920
I'm guessing that Law
isn't the mastermind here.

361
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:02,340
Someone else is.

362
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:04,480
Someone with the initial CC.

363
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:07,080
And I think I know who.

364
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,460
It would make sense.

365
00:18:10,940 --> 00:18:13,220
Him being here on this island.

366
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:18,620
A lot of things are
starting to fall into place.

367
00:18:27,620 --> 00:18:31,300
I believe the person behind this
is a former colleague of Dr.

368
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:36,000
Vegapunk A scientist named Caesar Clown

369
00:18:38,540 --> 00:18:40,716
Heavens, what have you done now, Law?

370
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:41,810
Well

371
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:48,720
If anyone's got a complaint, it's me

372
00:18:49,580 --> 00:18:50,410
Caesar.

373
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:07,220
I think I have some
information that might help.

374
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:08,730
Huh?

375
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:12,700
I noticed something unusual a while back.

376
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:15,137
Suspicious reports from this area.

377
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:18,477
A lot of reports, all of them
concerning child abduction.

378
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:20,442
You mean like a kidnapping ring?

379
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:21,750
Yes.

380
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:27,957
I don't know if I can handle this, Cap!

381
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:29,757
It's like you're not you anymore!

382
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,277
You've got to suck it up, Marine.

383
00:19:31,360 --> 00:19:32,917
We're stuck like this for now.

384
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,157
All right, Toshiki, get back on track.

385
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:38,997
These reports you're talking about,
why haven't I heard of them before?

386
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:41,457
Please button up, I can't
even look at myself!

387
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:43,417
There's something wrong
about seeing her like this!

388
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:46,177
I know I shouldn't like
it, but God help me, I do!

389
00:19:46,260 --> 00:19:47,090
That's enough!

390
00:19:48,760 --> 00:19:53,180
I have noticed that accidents at sea
happen fairly frequently in this area.

391
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:58,100
And it does seem that an unusual
number involved children.

392
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:01,900
Oh, yeah, that's true. Right? Yeah.

393
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:04,837
The thing is, per the
communication department...

394
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:06,540
Oh, right, no glasses.

395
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:10,977
Well, from what I've heard, we get
a whole lot of abduction reports.

396
00:20:11,060 --> 00:20:15,377
But somehow they always end up labeled
in the newspaper as accidents at sea,

397
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:18,048
the work of pirates,
or simply a lost child.

398
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:22,320
And I guess it's possible the
incidents are reported incorrectly.

399
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:24,630
Possible.

400
00:20:25,220 --> 00:20:29,880
But unfortunately to me it seems
far more likely that, well...

401
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:35,645
Are you going to finish
your sentence, Tashigi?

402
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:40,737
come on saying it out
loud won't change anything

403
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:44,597
we all know we saw a bunch
of kids on the island

404
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:48,737
earlier what you're too
afraid to say is you think

405
00:20:48,820 --> 00:20:51,526
there really have been
a series of kidnappings

406
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:55,160
and you believe the perpetrator
is here on punk hazard

407
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:01,760
but if your suspicions
about that are correct

408
00:21:06,260 --> 00:21:09,397
those news articles
weren't simple mistakes the

409
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:12,377
reporters were deliberately
misled because someone in g5

410
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:15,517
wanted those abduction
reports covered up hold on

411
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:18,377
is smoky saying that somebody
in our ranks is working

412
00:21:18,460 --> 00:21:21,497
with the kidnapper what
the hell smokey happy for

413
00:21:21,580 --> 00:21:24,337
a soldier crew like that
sure we're not the smartest

414
00:21:24,420 --> 00:21:26,937
or strongest marines there
are but that doesn't change

415
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:29,477
the fact that We just tried
to be part of the maze!

416
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:31,060
Quit your bitching!

417
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:32,540
Don't hurt us!

418
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:35,117
You fools couldn't
steal candy from a baby.

419
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:36,857
You're not even worth suspecting.

420
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:37,770
What?

421
00:21:38,060 --> 00:21:39,960
But don't let loyalty blind you.

422
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:42,811
Not even the Navy is immune to corruption.

423
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:47,080
At the end of the day, the
Navy is just a group of people.

424
00:21:47,380 --> 00:21:48,909
And people aren't perfect.

425
00:21:49,420 --> 00:21:51,302
Making assumptions is dangerous.

426
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:53,640
Don't be fooled by appearances.

427
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:55,240
Ah! Oh!

428
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,460
understood captain

429
00:22:09,180 --> 00:22:15,137
never mind morons um guys
i'm the captain right sorry

430
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:19,197
we're still getting used to
this i could still be wrong i

431
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:22,237
don't have any proof it's a
theory that's all that doesn't

432
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:25,791
matter theory or not it's
something we need to keep in mind

433
00:22:25,980 --> 00:22:30,077
Unfortunately, as it stands, my heart
and both our bodies are at law's mercy.

434
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:32,377
We're both stuck here till we settle that.

435
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:36,777
But I want a third of you to leave by
ship and report what we've found so far.

436
00:22:36,860 --> 00:22:38,937
Just one problem with that, Vice Admiral.

437
00:22:39,020 --> 00:22:41,517
If you remember, our
warship was destroyed.

438
00:22:41,600 --> 00:22:43,940
I told you I saw a ship, didn't I?

439
00:22:44,540 --> 00:22:45,800
Steal it. Oh, yeah!

440
00:22:45,980 --> 00:22:47,317
I hadn't thought of that!

441
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:48,257
Stealing's bad, though!

442
00:22:48,340 --> 00:22:49,634
Just do it, all right?

443
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:51,860
And be careful nobody catches you.

444
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:54,777
Meanwhile, I'm going to find a
way to get my heart and body back.

445
00:22:54,860 --> 00:22:58,154
and hunt down the twisted
bastard who's behind all this.

446
00:23:03,400 --> 00:23:06,180
I was finally able to get through to him.

447
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:09,600
We have permission to kill them all.

448
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:15,080
The Straw Hat Pirates, the G5
crew, Foxfire Kin'emon as well.

449
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:17,380
No matter who dies on this island,

450
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:21,856
Joker will ensure the losses are
officially listed as accidents at sea.

451
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:24,120
Catch as many of them as possible.

452
00:23:24,860 --> 00:23:26,777
The more guinea pigs, the merrier.

453
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:27,760
Yes, master.

454
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:33,073
I prefer them alive, but you may kill
any that can't be taken with poison.

455
00:23:33,460 --> 00:23:34,880
Where did Law go?

456
00:23:35,140 --> 00:23:37,199
He left the room a few minutes ago.

457
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:38,700
Well, be careful.

458
00:23:39,080 --> 00:23:41,220
These pirates have large bounties.

459
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:43,120
One is 400 million.

460
00:23:43,500 --> 00:23:46,620
The others range from 50
berries to 120 million.

461
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:51,215
All are wanted, and their total
bounties are 800 million and 50 berries.

462
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:55,877
They're notorious despite the fact they've
been enacted for the past two years.

463
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:58,577
Their bounties haven't
increased in that time.

464
00:23:58,660 --> 00:24:01,601
They could be more powerful
than the numbers show.

465
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:04,440
You're ever the font
of information, Monet.

466
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:07,020
Help, Master!

467
00:24:08,460 --> 00:24:09,290
Huh?

468
00:24:10,380 --> 00:24:11,920
You look half frozen.

469
00:24:12,380 --> 00:24:15,137
Have you been wandering
around outside without a coat?

470
00:24:15,220 --> 00:24:17,097
We were robbed by pirates, Master.

471
00:24:17,180 --> 00:24:21,217
Master, what's worse is that the scheming
lowlights took Boss Brownbeard with them.

472
00:24:21,300 --> 00:24:23,377
Please, Master, we have to help him.

473
00:24:23,460 --> 00:24:24,290
Really?

474
00:24:24,373 --> 00:24:25,392
How absolutely terrible.

475
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:28,400
Don't worry about Brownbeard.

476
00:24:28,900 --> 00:24:31,240
I promise you we will retrieve him.

477
00:24:31,420 --> 00:24:33,100
Now go on back to the room.

478
00:24:33,700 --> 00:24:35,680
As it happens, you're in luck.

479
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:38,019
We've just finished a new medicine.

480
00:24:38,600 --> 00:24:39,757
Exactly what you need.

481
00:24:39,840 --> 00:24:42,740
It will both warm and heal you. Really?

482
00:24:43,040 --> 00:24:44,220
That's so kind.

483
00:24:44,760 --> 00:24:45,917
Will you help the others too?

484
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:48,320
Sure, certainly.

485
00:24:48,820 --> 00:24:50,761
But first, let's get you treated.

486
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:53,740
You do so much for us, Master.

487
00:24:54,080 --> 00:24:56,000
I don't know how to repay you.

488
00:24:57,480 --> 00:24:58,600
Are you kidding?

489
00:24:58,760 --> 00:25:00,317
What the hell is this, Usopp?

490
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:02,420
I think you're totally super, bro.

491
00:25:03,340 --> 00:25:04,640
I don't care anymore.

492
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,200
Thanks, Usopp!

493
00:25:06,300 --> 00:25:07,140
Great idea!

494
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:10,134
This thing detracts from Nami's beauty.

495
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:11,800
Ah, quit whining.

496
00:25:12,180 --> 00:25:15,397
Without some sort of system like this,
we're never going to remember who's who.

497
00:25:15,480 --> 00:25:16,892
It's a Brownbeard, huh?

498
00:25:17,940 --> 00:25:18,770
That's right.

499
00:25:18,853 --> 00:25:20,497
I'm sure you've heard that name.

500
00:25:20,580 --> 00:25:22,109
It's what I used to go by.

501
00:25:22,520 --> 00:25:23,380
Nope, sorry.

502
00:25:23,700 --> 00:25:25,229
Are you kidding, you fool?

503
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:26,557
Something's up.

504
00:25:26,640 --> 00:25:29,837
You wouldn't say a word before,
and now you won't stop yapping.

505
00:25:29,920 --> 00:25:32,449
Why are you so eager
to run your mouth now?

506
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:33,470
Oh-ho.

507
00:25:33,553 --> 00:25:36,157
I'm in a good mood because
you guys are in for it.

508
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:38,997
Law knows that I'm with you
now, and he's gonna come for me.

509
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:42,609
I despise all the worthless
pirates of your damn generation.

510
00:25:43,060 --> 00:25:45,100
Law's the exception. Hold on.

511
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,217
What do you mean, our generation?

512
00:25:47,300 --> 00:25:49,540
Don't you know anything, little fool?

513
00:25:50,580 --> 00:25:53,537
I mean the 11 rookies
with bounties over 100

514
00:25:53,620 --> 00:25:56,400
million who arrived at
Sabaody two years ago.

515
00:25:56,860 --> 00:25:58,780
You lot and Blackbeard.

516
00:25:59,320 --> 00:26:01,920
People call you puns the worst generation.

517
00:26:02,500 --> 00:26:05,497
Troublemakers who were born
at the change of the era.

518
00:26:05,580 --> 00:26:09,639
Reckless fools whose actions will
determine the future of this world.

519
00:26:10,020 --> 00:26:14,237
After Whitebeard died, you all came to
the new world and began raising hell.

520
00:26:14,320 --> 00:26:16,280
Anytime something big happened,

521
00:26:16,420 --> 00:26:20,479
a member of your generation was
usually right in the thick of things.

522
00:26:21,760 --> 00:26:25,920
Blackbeard, Kid, Law, Drake, and Hawkins.

523
00:26:27,220 --> 00:26:31,926
Basil Hawkins was the one who shattered
my crew, leaving us defeated and broken.

524
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:35,581
It was because of him that
my pirate career ended.

525
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:37,722
The coward took my legs from me.

526
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:39,460
My crew was annihilated.

527
00:26:39,820 --> 00:26:42,917
I was fleeing for my life
when at last I arrived here.

528
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:46,000
on the island known as Punk Hazard.

529
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:50,000
Do you fools even know
what this place is? Huh?

530
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:56,300
This island is not what it was.

531
00:26:57,140 --> 00:27:00,380
It used to be a paradise
teeming with life,

532
00:27:00,540 --> 00:27:02,957
home to creatures of
all shapes and colors.

533
00:27:03,040 --> 00:27:03,870
Wow, for real?

534
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:05,824
It's nothing like that anymore.

535
00:27:06,080 --> 00:27:10,797
This island housed a laboratory of a
government scientist known as Dr. Vegapunk.

536
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:13,817
He and his team were
stationed here with the

537
00:27:13,900 --> 00:27:16,547
task of developing new
chemicals and weapons.

538
00:27:20,740 --> 00:27:23,917
Vegapunk needed subjects on
which to test his inventions,

539
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:25,800
so instead of going to prison,

540
00:27:26,040 --> 00:27:29,452
criminals were sent here, where
they were experimented on.

541
00:27:30,360 --> 00:27:34,948
Four years ago, Vegapunk tested one of
his chemical weapons, and it went very,

542
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:35,950
very wrong.

543
00:27:58,840 --> 00:28:02,252
Two of the three labs exploded,
destroyed almost entirely.

544
00:28:03,060 --> 00:28:06,220
We are standing in the
remains of one right now.

545
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:14,900
That makes sense.

546
00:28:15,180 --> 00:28:17,597
A huge explosion would
do this kind of damage,

547
00:28:17,680 --> 00:28:19,940
so Robin's theory was right after all.

548
00:28:20,220 --> 00:28:23,396
Intense heat and toxic
substances seeped into the air,

549
00:28:23,520 --> 00:28:26,873
and none of the plants or
animals on the island survived.

550
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:38,320
Vegapunk's operation was shut down, and his
guinea pigs were thrown away like trash.

551
00:28:39,900 --> 00:28:42,018
They did what they could to survive,

552
00:28:42,160 --> 00:28:45,219
taking shelter in the third
laboratory, the only one

553
00:28:45,500 --> 00:28:46,330
still intact.

554
00:28:46,413 --> 00:28:51,042
There, they were protected from the poison
gas that contaminated the entire island.

555
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:54,671
Those who survived were paralyzed
from exposure to the gas,

556
00:28:54,760 --> 00:28:56,760
which stole the use of their lower

557
00:28:57,220 --> 00:28:58,050
bodies.

558
00:28:58,133 --> 00:29:01,140
They lived on, without any
real hope for the future.

559
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:04,120
But then, a year later, everything

560
00:29:04,800 --> 00:29:05,630
changed.

561
00:29:05,713 --> 00:29:09,340
A kind master arrived on the island,
restoring the hope that had been

562
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:10,830
lost.

563
00:29:10,913 --> 00:29:14,420
With his ability, he purified
the island of the toxic gas.

564
00:29:14,820 --> 00:29:19,157
He also gave the prisoners who couldn't
walk the mechanical means to move.

565
00:29:19,240 --> 00:29:23,880
More than that, he gave them purpose
by making them his loyal subordinates.

566
00:29:25,840 --> 00:29:27,120
Kind master!

567
00:29:27,940 --> 00:29:28,770
Master!

568
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:30,680
Merciful master!

569
00:29:31,520 --> 00:29:35,520
I came to the island a year
after that, desperate and broken.

570
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:38,214
Two years have passed since my arrival.

571
00:29:50,740 --> 00:29:54,060
Some toxic substances
remained in the air even then,

572
00:29:54,320 --> 00:29:56,849
and breathing had left
me feeling nauseous.

573
00:29:56,980 --> 00:30:00,280
I began to think I had no
more strength to carry on.

574
00:30:00,680 --> 00:30:03,820
I had fought to survive,
but I was reaching the end.

575
00:30:09,680 --> 00:30:14,268
But then I saw them, the men who had
lost the use of their legs just as I had.

576
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:17,780
And with them, the Master.

577
00:30:19,080 --> 00:30:20,640
I owe everything to him.

578
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:24,660
His kindness saved my life
as it saved others before me.

579
00:30:25,520 --> 00:30:28,697
Vega Punk and his experiments
stole my comrade's legs.

580
00:30:28,780 --> 00:30:30,717
But then the master arrived.

581
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:33,260
A kind and generous savior.

582
00:30:34,200 --> 00:30:37,817
And then a few months ago fate
brought us another surprise.

583
00:30:37,900 --> 00:30:39,377
Trafalgar Law.

584
00:30:39,460 --> 00:30:43,480
A warlord arrived on the island
and became our second savior.

585
00:30:44,980 --> 00:30:46,657
Using his special ability.

586
00:30:46,740 --> 00:30:50,957
He gave legs to those of us who couldn't
walk without mechanical assistance.

587
00:30:51,040 --> 00:30:53,640
They were the legs of living animals.

588
00:30:59,620 --> 00:31:01,800
We thought we would never walk again?

589
00:31:02,020 --> 00:31:04,432
so we wept when our bodies were restored.

590
00:31:05,420 --> 00:31:08,460
Oh, my God, that's the
most beautiful story ever!

591
00:31:08,860 --> 00:31:11,331
You see, I told you Traffy was a good guy.

592
00:31:11,420 --> 00:31:13,757
I'm not the only one whose life he saved.

593
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:14,800
How could Dr.

594
00:31:14,900 --> 00:31:16,697
Vegapunk do something so horrible?

595
00:31:16,780 --> 00:31:21,017
Well, I guess this explains the half-sheep
people, the ones back at the laboratory.

596
00:31:21,100 --> 00:31:22,317
Centaurs and the Bird Woman.

597
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:26,220
It all makes sense now, except
the dragon. What's up with that?

598
00:31:26,500 --> 00:31:27,380
Ah, yes.

599
00:31:27,620 --> 00:31:29,032
Saw the dragon, did you?

600
00:31:29,380 --> 00:31:31,677
That's just an artificial
creature Vegapunk

601
00:31:31,760 --> 00:31:34,760
created to guard the island
from unwanted visitors.

602
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:38,060
It can adapt to any
environment imaginable.

603
00:31:38,300 --> 00:31:41,577
I heard one of the world nobles
liked it and gave it a name.

604
00:31:41,660 --> 00:31:45,440
I forgot what it was,
but run if you see it.

605
00:31:45,560 --> 00:31:47,140
It's very aggressive.

606
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:48,720
I'm not worried.

607
00:31:48,900 --> 00:31:49,897
We already ate it.

608
00:31:49,980 --> 00:31:53,627
Now you know who's in charge on
the island and why we're here.

609
00:31:54,100 --> 00:31:56,197
Nobody else dares to come near it now.

610
00:31:56,280 --> 00:31:57,751
It belongs to the Master.

611
00:31:58,220 --> 00:32:00,573
Punk hazard is the domain of our savior.

612
00:32:02,280 --> 00:32:03,600
No, don't cry.

613
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:07,685
The Master continues his research
for the betterment of mankind.

614
00:32:07,820 --> 00:32:09,761
To do so, he needs test subjects,

615
00:32:09,900 --> 00:32:12,959
and each of you will have
the honor of becoming one.

616
00:32:13,660 --> 00:32:16,340
Like it or not, you're his.

617
00:32:19,820 --> 00:32:20,650
Hmm?

618
00:32:20,733 --> 00:32:22,740
Is something the matter? Master!

619
00:32:23,220 --> 00:32:25,260
Master, I can't breathe!

620
00:32:25,620 --> 00:32:29,100
What kind of medicine is this?

621
00:32:31,300 --> 00:32:32,580
Please, Master!

622
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:35,190
Master!

623
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:40,600
Please just let me out of here!

624
00:32:41,900 --> 00:32:44,240
I need you to hang on a little longer.

625
00:32:44,860 --> 00:32:46,560
Describe how you feel.

626
00:32:49,120 --> 00:32:52,157
From the sound of it, there's
some nausea and coughing.

627
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:54,540
Does your head hurt as well? Yes.

628
00:32:54,800 --> 00:32:59,160
It feels like it's going
to split open. Yes. Yes.

629
00:32:59,420 --> 00:33:00,320
I see.

630
00:33:01,660 --> 00:33:02,490
What?

631
00:33:02,573 --> 00:33:03,920
It wasn't Vegapunk?

632
00:33:04,140 --> 00:33:05,660
But he was in charge.

633
00:33:06,080 --> 00:33:09,277
If Vegapunk didn't cause that
huge explosion, who did, Smokey?

634
00:33:09,360 --> 00:33:13,157
The person who made the weapon
and accidentally set it off.

635
00:33:13,240 --> 00:33:15,460
That was Caesar Clown.

636
00:33:17,940 --> 00:33:20,260
He and Vegapunk worked together.

637
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:23,040
Caesar Clown was second in command here.

638
00:33:23,320 --> 00:33:26,438
But because of his tendency
towards inhumane methods,

639
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:29,080
he and Vegapunk butted heads frequently.

640
00:33:30,180 --> 00:33:31,900
Please, please, Master.

641
00:33:34,480 --> 00:33:36,620
Please help me.

642
00:33:38,840 --> 00:33:41,240
How are your eyes doing?

643
00:33:41,520 --> 00:33:42,932
Are you seeing anything?

644
00:33:43,240 --> 00:33:44,070
Strange

645
00:33:53,680 --> 00:33:54,510
Too bad.

646
00:33:54,740 --> 00:33:56,037
All right, that's enough.

647
00:33:56,120 --> 00:33:56,960
Goodbye now

648
00:34:04,840 --> 00:34:07,977
After the accident happened
Vegapunk was listed as

649
00:34:08,060 --> 00:34:11,820
responsible because he was the
person in charge Of course,

650
00:34:12,140 --> 00:34:14,677
it was a crime to develop
a chemical weapon of mass

651
00:34:14,760 --> 00:34:17,337
destruction that could
take out an entire island.

652
00:34:17,420 --> 00:34:22,302
When Caesar Clown's involvement came to
light after the explosion, he was arrested.

653
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:27,560
But, using his formidable ability,
he escaped from a prison ship.

654
00:34:27,860 --> 00:34:30,213
And his location has been unknown since.

655
00:34:30,740 --> 00:34:33,257
If my suspicions are correct and Caesar is

656
00:34:33,340 --> 00:34:36,164
back here on this island
conducting experiments,

657
00:34:36,640 --> 00:34:40,157
we have to stop him
before he does something.

658
00:34:40,240 --> 00:34:42,180
even more horrible than before.

659
00:34:43,700 --> 00:34:44,800
Giant snake.

660
00:34:49,720 --> 00:34:52,160
Was this one another failure? Huh?

661
00:34:53,120 --> 00:34:54,260
Failure, you say?

662
00:34:54,660 --> 00:34:56,778
You really should watch your tongue.

663
00:34:57,200 --> 00:35:01,494
My experiments are never failures,
not even what happened four years ago.

664
00:35:02,240 --> 00:35:05,537
None of the useless idiots in the world
government know what they're talking

665
00:35:05,620 --> 00:35:10,780
about a failed experiment i developed
a weapon that killed an entire island

666
00:35:11,760 --> 00:35:14,997
how is that anything
but a success i proved

667
00:35:15,080 --> 00:35:17,797
myself the most efficient
killer in the world

668
00:35:17,880 --> 00:35:22,017
didn't i i meticulously
document each of my

669
00:35:22,100 --> 00:35:24,571
victims until they draw their final breath

670
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:29,037
just you wait soon it
will be my day and they'll

671
00:35:29,120 --> 00:35:31,708
know i'm the greatest
scientist to ever live

672
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:43,117


673
00:35:43,200 --> 00:35:43,253
Thank you.
